          "hitHighlights" : {
            "dc.description.abstract" : [ "To fill this gap in the literature, we adopt the framework proposed by Steinmetz and Jentsch (2022) to derive <em>asymptotic</em> <em>theory</em> in <em>Mack</em>&#x27;s model. By splitting the reserve into two parts corresponding to process and estimation uncertainty, this enables - for the first time - a rigorous investigation also of the validity of the <em>Mack</em> bootstrap. We prove that the (conditional) distribution of the <em>asymptotically</em> dominating process uncertainty part is correctly mimicked by <em>Mack</em>&#x27;s bootstrap if the parametric family of distributions of the individual development factors is correctly specified. " ]
